      "id": "NL-001",
      "screenID": "fog-and-ice",
      "level": 3,
      "severity": "minor",
      "required": true,
      "category": "Incorrect chronology / invented causal transition",
      "location": "copy.ru.body and copy.en.body; identical in authoring, both connected manuscripts and effective HTML",
      "exactClause": {
        "ru": "Но разговор обрывается опасностью.",
        "en": "Danger ends their conversation."
      },
      "replacementSpan": {
        "ru": {
          "before": "Но разговор обрывается опасностью. На шар нападают скальные призраки.",
          "after": "Позже на шар нападают скальные призраки."
        },
        "en": {
          "before": "Danger ends their conversation. Cliff-ghasts attack the balloon.",
          "after": "Later, cliff-ghasts attack the balloon."
        }
      },
      "reason": "This says the attack interrupts Lyra’s conversation with Serafina. The consulted chapter prose instead ends the discussion with Lyra becoming too tired, then places her awakening and the attack later. Omitting sleep is legitimate compression; changing what ends the conversation introduces a false causal link. The attack, fall and capture otherwise need no change.",
      "evidence": {
        "url": "https://zigzageducation.co.uk/samplepdf/English/s5161.pdf#page=84",
        "title": "Helen Mason / ZigZag Education official guide",
        "novelChapter": 18,
        "chapterTitle": "Fog and Ice",
        "guidePrintedPage": 79,
        "pdfPage1Based": 84,
        "webTextLines": "2945–2951",
        "kind": "Declarative prose chapter summary, not a teacher question",
        "paraphrase": "The discussion ends in tiredness; subsequently the balloon’s violent movement wakes Lyra before the cliff-ghast attack and fall.",
        "limit": "This correction is supported within the substantial guide’s scope; it is not a claim of a complete primary reading of chapter 18."
      },
      "smallestSupportedCorrection": "Replace only the two leading sentences with the supplied Later/Позже sentence. No added scene, dialogue, motive or new screen is needed.",
